GPSA provides fast similarity search over large-scale perturbation signature databases using cMAP/GSEA-style rankZ semantics. It supports single gene-set queries, up/down bidirectional queries, multi-channel event definitions, batch queries, and vector-based full geneList searches. HDF5-based storage enables memory-efficient querying with optional preloading for maximum speed (~0.15s per query in memory mode).
